<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>Warning - BigFix Root Server has a long Evaluation Cycle - Windows</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P>This Fixlet is relevant when the&nbsp;BigFix Root has an evaluation cycle of longer than 40 minutes. An evaluation cycle of longer than 20 minutes is indicative of poor root server performance.</P>
<P>This means that existing Fixlets/Tasks/Analyses will be slow to show as applicable and slow to report results.</P>
<P>You can solve this by either:</P>
<OL>
<LI>Increasing the CPU Usage of the BigFix Agent on the Root Server (Using Fixlet 168 in BES Support: <?relevance links of fixlet 168 of all bes sites whose (name of it = "BES Support")?>, setting to High or Very High). For concerns about raising the CPU Usage please see the notes below.
<LI>Review the evaluation cycles and determine&nbsp;what the root server&nbsp;is spending its time on.</LI></OL>
<P><FONT color=#ff0000><STRONG>CPU Usage Notes:</STRONG></FONT>&nbsp;</P>
<P>The BigFix Agent is often said to consume 2% CPU and this is a bit of&nbsp;a misnomer -- the default agent settings mean that it will indeed consume 2% CPU but because the agent is single-threaded the most it will ever consume is 2% of a single CPU Core. This means on an 8 core server the agent actually consumes 0.25% of total CPU and on a 16 core server the agent consumes 0.125% of total CPU.</P>
<P>Increasing the CPU Usage of the agent on the root server will make it significantly more responsive and, because the agent is limited to one CPU, raising it to even 25% or 50% on the root server is unlikely to impact any services on the server itself.</P>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>exists main gather service</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[(average of evaluationcycle of client / 1000 / 60) > 40]]></Relevance>
    <Category>Audit</Category>
    <Source>Internal</Source>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2016-12-05</SourceReleaseDate>
    <SourceSeverity>Critical</SourceSeverity>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Sun, 11 Sep 2016 22:05:56 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
